#: ../../../building-testing.rst:2
msgid "Building and Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:4
msgid ""
"To use Highlight.js it is first necessary to build it for the environment "
"where you plan to execute it: the browser, the Node.js server, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:8
msgid "TLDR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:10
msgid ""
"Often when contributing a pull-request it's sufficient to build and test "
"only the Node.js build. Our CI process will guarantee the browser build "
"tests are all still green if you don't run them during development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:16
msgid ""
"npm run build\n"
"npm run test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:19
msgid "The browser library must be built and tested separately:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:23
msgid ""
"npm run build-browser\n"
"npm run test-browser"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:27
msgid "Building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:29
msgid ""
"The build tool is written in JavaScript using node.js. Before running the "
"script, make sure to have node installed and run ``npm install`` to get the "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:33
msgid "The tool is located in ``tools/build.js``. A few useful examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:35
msgid "Build for a browser using only common languages::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:37
msgid "node tools/build.js :common"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:39
msgid "Build for node.js including all available languages::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:41
msgid "node tools/build.js -t node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:43
msgid ""
"Build two specific languages for debugging, skipping compression in this "
"case::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:45
msgid "node tools/build.js -n python ruby"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:47
msgid ""
"On some systems the node binary is named ``nodejs``; simply replace ``node`` "
"with ``nodejs`` in the examples above if that is the case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:50
msgid ""
"The full option reference is available with the usual ``--help`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:52
msgid "The build result will be in the ``build/`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:57
msgid "Basic testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:59
msgid ""
"The usual approach to debugging and testing a language is first doing it "
"visually. You need to build highlight.js with only the language you're "
"working on (without compression, to have readable code in browser error "
"messages) and then use the Developer tool in ``tools/developer.html`` to see "
"how it highlights a test snippet in that language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:65
msgid ""
"A test snippet should be short and give the idea of the overall look of the "
"language. It shouldn't include every possible syntactic element and "
"shouldn't even make practical sense."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:69
msgid ""
"After you satisfied with the result you need to make sure that language "
"detection still works with your language definition included in the whole "
"suite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:72
msgid ""
"Testing is done using `Mocha <http://mochajs.org/>`_ and the files are found "
"in the ``test/`` directory. You can use the node build to run the tests from "
"the command line with ``npm test`` after building_. (Using ``npm run "
"build_and_test`` you can build and then test with one command.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:77
msgid ""
"**Note**: for Debian-based machine, like Ubuntu, you might need to create an "
"alias or symbolic link for nodejs to node. The reason for this is the "
"dependencies that are requires to test highlight.js has a reference to "
"\"node\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:82
msgid ""
"Place the snippet you used inside the browser in ``test/detect/<language>/"
"default.txt``, build the package with all the languages for node and run the "
"test suite. If your language breaks auto-detection, it should be fixed by :"
"ref:`improving relevance <relevance>`, which is a black art in and of "
"itself. When in doubt, please refer to the discussion group!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:90
msgid "Testing markup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:92
msgid ""
"You can also provide additional markup tests for the language to test "
"isolated cases of various syntactic construct. If your language has 19 "
"different string literals or complicated heuristics for telling division (``/"
"``) apart from regexes (``/ .. /``) -- this is the place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:97
msgid "A test case consists of two files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:99
msgid "``test/markup/<language>/<test_name>.txt``: test code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:100
msgid "``test/markup/<language>/<test_name>.expect.txt``: reference rendering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:102
msgid ""
"To generate reference rendering use the Developer tool located at ``tools/"
"developer.html``. Make sure to explicitly select your language in the drop-"
"down menu, as automatic detection is unlikely to work in this case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:108
msgid "Building and Testing with Docker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:110
msgid ""
"If you don't want to install dependencies on your system, you can use the "
"included Dockerfile to build a container that will add the source code and "
"then deploy a web server for you to preview it. Specifically, after you "
"finish with your changes you can build the container from the root of the "
"repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:117
msgid "docker build -t highlight-js ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:120
msgid ""
"And then run the container. You will need to expose port 80 on the host for "
"the web interface, and note that we are running it in detached (-d) mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:125
msgid "docker run -d --name highlight-js --rm -p 80:80 highlight-js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:128
msgid "If your preference is for another port, you can do that too:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:133
msgid "docker run -d --name highlight-js --rm -p 80:8080 highlight-js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:136
msgid ""
"Or you can skip binding a port if your intention is to interactively shell "
"into the container to use it as a development environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:142
msgid "docker run -d --name highlight-js --rm highlight-js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:145
msgid "Whatever you choose, you can use docker ps to ensure that it's running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:149
msgid ""
"$ docker ps\n"
"CONTAINER ID        IMAGE               COMMAND                  "
"CREATED             STATUS              PORTS                NAMES\n"
"0e15a7c99adf        highlight-js        \"docker-entrypoint.s…\"   8 seconds "
"ago       Up 7 seconds        0.0.0.0:80->80/tcp   highlight-js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:154
msgid ""
"Then, open up to http://127.0.0.1/tools/developer.html to see the developer "
"page for preview. When you are done, clean up your container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:159
msgid "docker stop highlight-js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:161
msgid ""
"If you want a more advanced testing setup, you can bind the source folder "
"when you run the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:166
msgid ""
"docker run -d --name highlight-js --volume $PWD/src:/var/www/html/src --rm -"
"p 80:80 highlight-js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:168
msgid ""
"Then if you want to make changes, you can do so locally (the folder is bound "
"as a volume), and execute a command to the container to trigger a rebuild:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:173
msgid "docker exec highlight-js node tools/build.js :common"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../building-testing.rst:176
msgid ""
"And then reload the page to see changes. When you finish, don't forget to "
"remove the container."
msgstr ""
